  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Production volumes expanded as new Tishomingo field wells came online, with recent completions delivering high oil cuts and encouraging early rates. However, a softer commodity price environment eroded realized prices, causing revenue and earnings to contract despite growing output. The company’s concentrated Oklahoma oil exposure makes its performance sensitive to macro-driven pricing headwinds, which muted the benefit of operational momentum.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is pressing ahead aggressively, accelerating the drilling timeline for the three-well Clifton Mac pad and stepping up investment in the field. A successful increase in the credit-line borrowing base bolsters financial flexibility and signals lender confidence. These moves reflect a leadership team focused on volume-led growth and proactive capital management, maintaining momentum through the cycle even as weaker oil prices challenge near-term profitability.",
